Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:12:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] AWQ beside GPTQ: an AWQ solve on the same int4 grid,
 scaled norms carried through the export, and a driver that compares the two

pipeline/awq.py follows AutoAWQ (duo-scaled input scales per group of linears sharing an
input, folded into the RMSNorm or the linear before; clip search per linear) on the grid
solve.py solves: symmetric int4 in groups of 32, bf16 scales, int8 per-token activations.
export_with_codes applies the fp32 parameters a solve changed besides the int4 linears
(codes["__fp32__"]) before quantising, and refuses any that match no parameter.
scripts/awq_compare.py builds one fp32 reference per model, then solves, exports and
measures each method against it: the publish gate, and first-token and teacher-forced KL
on the phone benchmark's 141 held-out questions under the app's prompt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
